@notice Burn address used to permanently lock {BasketMath.MIN_LIQUIDITY}
         shares on the first mint.
 @dev OpenZeppelin ERC20 v5 reverts on `_mint(address(0), …)`, so we
      send the locked floor to the canonical 0xdead address. The shares
      are still part of `totalSupply` and so still anchor the
      `balance/totalSupply` ratios that protect existing holders.

@notice Minimum allowed window between `block.timestamp` and an
         async mint's `intentDeadline`. Prevents griefer-set deadlines
         that would force `cancelMint` to succeed too aggressively.

@notice Maximum allowed window between `block.timestamp` and an
         async mint's `intentDeadline`. Bounds how long a user's
         escrow can be locked in pending state.

@notice Canonical WETH address for the deployed network.
 @dev Set once in the implementation constructor; shared across all clones
      via delegatecall semantics.

@dev Sum of `syncDeltas[i]` across all pending intents, keyed by the
      slot's underlying token. Subtracted from live balances to derive
      the available basket balance.

@dev Per-slot virtual balance for async slots. Incremented at finalize
      by the attested amount; decremented at burnAsync by the pro-rata
      amount dispatched.

@dev Validates external inputs and populates `L.floor`, `L.n`, `L.tokens`.
      Pure validation: no state changes, no external calls except read-only
      view calls to the factory.

@dev Iterates each slot, dispatching sync slots through their adapters
      (escrowing the delta) and async slots through theirs (sending the
      funding allocation to the partner network via the adapter).

@dev Sync slot dispatch inside `mintAsync`. Mirrors the sync-mint per-slot
      logic: balance delta verification, funding-token-as-slot fast path,
      and the `delta != 0` invariant for first-mint compatibility.

@dev Post-dispatch invariant: funding remaining = before-dispatch
      balance - everything we transferred to adapters. Catches an
      adapter that pulled extra funding from this contract.

@dev Calls `cancelAcquire` on every async slot's adapter. The adapters
      emit events the off-chain executor uses to dedupe and reconcile.
      No on-chain funds move in this loop.

@dev Sync slots: ERC20 transfer to caller. Async slots: invoke
      `redeemAsync` on the adapter (carrying the user's native
      recipient bytes) and decrement the virtual slot balance.
